US English speaker who chose Argentine Spanish, at A2, on the same Coyoacán call. Their vos forms ("sabés", "podés") are correct Argentine Spanish: calling one a mistake, or changing it to "tú" or "usted" in "better", is a major error. The fix should be "es disponible" to "está disponible", explaining that availability is a state and takes "estar", with "better" keeping their vos ("¿Vos sabés si el departamento está disponible?"). "Went well" can quote "¿Cuánto es la renta?" or "el sábado a las cinco me viene bien". In US English.